  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disaster Risk Financing III (DRF III) &#x2013; Start Ready Risk Pool</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: A locally-led humanitarian system that anticipates and responds proactively to predictable and recurring hazards, expanding the reach of pre-positioned funding across diverse regions and risks to protect lives, enhance recovery, and uphold the dignity and resilience of communities at risk.OUTCOME: Increased coverage and accessibility of national DRF systems through the annual Start Ready Risk Pool, enabling anticipatory action and rapid response to predictable hazards, ultimately protecting more people from disaster impacts.OUTPUT 1: Pre-positioned funding via DRF and SR enables rapid disbursement of funds, facilitating efficient action before the risk season to enable timely and effective implementation of anticipatory action and early action.OUTPUT 2: DRF systems are co-created through an evidence-based process with active collaboration from diverse local and national stakeholders to strengthen and refine DRF systems.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Disaster Risk Financing III (DRF III) project, delivered through the Start Ready Risk Pool mechanism, is a locally-led humanitarian system that anticipates and responds proactively to predictable and recurring hazards. It expands the reach of pre-positioned funding across diverse regions and risks to protect lives, enhance recovery, and uphold the dignity and resilience of communities at risk. The programme operates through an annual Start Ready Risk Pool, enabling anticipatory action and rapid response ahead of predictable hazards, and is funded primarily by FCDO (UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office).</narrative>
  </description>
